{"slug":"k3d-cluster","title":"Create a local Kubernetes cluster with k3d","description":"The same journey with k3d, plus live node add and remove, a load balancer, ingress, metrics and a built-in registry.","order":4,"tags":["k3d"],"date":"2026-10-14","minutes":16,"words":1296,"toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"kind-or-k3d","text":"kind or k3d?"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-1--prepare-the-machine","text":"Part 1 — Prepare the machine"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-2--create-the-cluster","text":"Part 2 — Create the cluster"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-3--switch-to-the-cluster","text":"Part 3 — Switch to the cluster"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-4--the-nodes","text":"Part 4 — The nodes"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-5--namespaces","text":"Part 5 — Namespaces"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-6--what-k3d-gives-you-that-kind-does-not","text":"Part 6 — What k3d gives you that kind does not"},{"depth":3,"id":"61-reach-an-app-with-ingress-or-a-loadbalancer","text":"6.1 Reach an app with Ingress or a LoadBalancer"},{"depth":3,"id":"62-metrics-and-pod-autoscaling","text":"6.2 Metrics and pod autoscaling"},{"depth":3,"id":"63-your-own-images","text":"6.3 Your own images"},{"depth":3,"id":"64-dashboard","text":"6.4 Dashboard"},{"depth":2,"id":"part-7--stop-start-delete","text":"Part 7 — Stop, start, delete"}],"html":"<p>The same journey as <a href=\"/blog/kind-cluster\">Create a local Kubernetes cluster with kind</a>, with k3d instead of kind: install,\ncreate the cluster <code>local-cluster-1</code>, switch kubectl to it, look at the nodes, make namespaces. Then the extras\nthat make k3d feel more like a managed cloud cluster (GKE): adding and removing nodes live, a load balancer,\ningress, metrics, a built-in registry and a dashboard.</p>\n<p>k3d runs <strong>k3s</strong>, a small certified Kubernetes, inside Docker. Each node is a Docker container, as with kind.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Not tested yet.</strong> Written from k3d&#39;s documented behaviour. Run it once and fix anything that differs\n(<code>k3d &lt;command&gt; --help</code> shows the exact flags for your version).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>New to the words (node, context, namespace)? See <a href=\"/blog/concepts\">Concepts: what each piece is</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"kind-or-k3d\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#kind-or-k3d\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>kind or k3d?</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table (scrolls sideways)\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>kind</th><th>k3d</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Add or remove a node on a running cluster</td><td>no, re-create the cluster</td><td>yes, <code>k3d node create</code> / <code>delete</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Load balancer, ingress, metrics-server</td><td>install them yourself</td><td>bundled with k3s</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Local registry</td><td>a few manual steps</td><td>one flag</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Kubernetes</td><td>upstream, as it ships</td><td>k3s, lighter and faster to start</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Context name</td><td><code>kind-&lt;name&gt;</code></td><td><code>k3d-&lt;name&gt;</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Everything you learn about kubectl, namespaces, Deployments, Services and <code>nodeSelector</code> is the same on both.</p>\n<p>The names used throughout:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table (scrolls sideways)\"><table><thead><tr><th>Thing</th><th>Name</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cluster</td><td><code>local-cluster-1</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>kubectl context</td><td><code>k3d-local-cluster-1</code> (k3d always adds the <code>k3d-</code> prefix)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Nodes</td><td><code>k3d-local-cluster-1-server-0</code>, <code>k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-0</code>, <code>k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Load balancer container</td><td><code>k3d-local-cluster-1-serverlb</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Registry container</td><td><code>k3d-local-registry</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Namespaces</td><td><code>web</code>, <code>cache</code>, <code>db</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>k3s calls the control-plane a <strong>server</strong> and a worker an <strong>agent</strong>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-1--prepare-the-machine\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-1--prepare-the-machine\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 1 — Prepare the machine</h2>\n<p><strong>1.1 Start Docker</strong> and give it enough memory, as in Part 1 of\n<a href=\"/blog/kind-cluster\">Create a local Kubernetes cluster with kind</a>: roughly 4 GB or more for three nodes.</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20info%20--format%20'%7B%7B.ServerVersion%7D%7D'%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker info --format <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;{{.ServerVersion}}&#x27;</span></code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>1.2 Install the tools:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>brew install k3d</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>brew install --cask headlamp</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>k3d</code> makes the cluster. <code>headlamp</code> is a desktop dashboard that reads your kubeconfig (used in Part 6). You\nalso need <code>kubectl</code>: <code>brew install kubectl</code> if <code>kubectl version --client</code> does not work.</p>\n<p><strong>Check:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20version%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d version</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Prints the k3d and k3s versions.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-2--create-the-cluster\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-2--create-the-cluster\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 2 — Create the cluster</h2>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20create%20local-cluster-1%20--servers%201%20--agents%202%20--port%20%5C%228080%3A80%40loadbalancer%5C%22%20--registry-create%20local-registry%3A0.0.0.0%3A5001%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster create local-cluster-1 --servers 1 --agents 2 --port <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;8080:80@loadbalancer&quot;</span> --registry-create local-registry:0.0.0.0:5001</code></pre></figure>\n<p>If your terminal wraps long lines, paste it in the shorter form, with <code>\\</code> at the line ends:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20create%20local-cluster-1%20%5C%5C%22%2C%22%20%20--servers%201%20--agents%202%20%5C%5C%22%2C%22%20%20--port%20%5C%228080%3A80%40loadbalancer%5C%22%20%5C%5C%22%2C%22%20%20--registry-create%20local-registry%3A0.0.0.0%3A5001%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster create local-cluster-1 \\\n  --servers 1 --agents 2 \\\n  --port <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;8080:80@loadbalancer&quot;</span> \\\n  --registry-create local-registry:0.0.0.0:5001</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Flag by flag:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>local-cluster-1</code> — the cluster name.</li>\n<li><code>--servers 1</code> — one control-plane node. <code>--agents 2</code> — two worker nodes.</li>\n<li><code>--port &quot;8080:80@loadbalancer&quot;</code> — local port 8080 → port 80 on the cluster&#39;s load balancer. This is how you\nreach Ingress and LoadBalancer Services from the browser, with no <code>port-forward</code>. Like kind&#39;s\n<code>extraPortMappings</code>, it is set at creation (add more <code>--port</code> flags for more ports).</li>\n<li><code>--registry-create local-registry:0.0.0.0:5001</code> — starts a registry container named <code>k3d-local-registry</code>,\npublished on local port 5001, and tells every node to use it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It takes about a minute and ends by switching your kubectl context.</p>\n<p><strong>Look at what Docker now has:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20ps%20--format%20'table%20%7B%7B.Names%7D%7D%5C%5Ct%7B%7B.Ports%7D%7D'%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker ps --format <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Ports}}&#x27;</span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Three node containers (<code>…-server-0</code>, <code>…-agent-0</code>, <code>…-agent-1</code>), the load balancer <code>…-serverlb</code>, and\n<code>k3d-local-registry</code>.</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20list%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster list</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>Check:</strong> <code>local-cluster-1</code> is listed with <code>1/1</code> servers and <code>2/2</code> agents.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-3--switch-to-the-cluster\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-3--switch-to-the-cluster\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 3 — Switch to the cluster</h2>\n<p>The context is <code>k3d-local-cluster-1</code>: k3d&#39;s prefix, the way kind&#39;s is <code>kind-</code>. How the names come about:\n<a href=\"/blog/concepts#names-kubeconfig-and-contexts\">Concepts: what each piece is</a>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If your kubeconfig also holds a cloud or work cluster, a command meant for your lab cluster will run against\nthat one when it is the current context. Always know the current context.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20get-contexts%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config get-contexts</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20current-context%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config current-context</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20config%20use-context%20k3d-local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl config use-context k3d-local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20cluster-info%20--context%20k3d-local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl cluster-info --context k3d-local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>To aim one command without switching: <code>kubectl --context k3d-local-cluster-1 get nodes</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Check:</strong> <code>kubectl config current-context</code> prints <code>k3d-local-cluster-1</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-4--the-nodes\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-4--the-nodes\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 4 — The nodes</h2>\n<p><strong>4.1 See them:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20nodes%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get nodes</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"text\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">text</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d-local-cluster-1-server-0   Ready   control-plane,master\nk3d-local-cluster-1-agent-0    Ready   &lt;none&gt;\nk3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1    Ready   &lt;none&gt;</code></pre></figure>\n<p>All three <code>Ready</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>4.2 One difference from kind.</strong> In kind, the control-plane node is tainted so your pods stay off it. In\nk3s the server node has no such taint by default, so your pods <strong>can</strong> be scheduled on it too. If you want them\nonly on the agents, taint the server:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20taint%20node%20k3d-local-cluster-1-server-0%20node-role.kubernetes.io%2Fcontrol-plane%3Dtrue%3ANoSchedule%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl taint node k3d-local-cluster-1-server-0 node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">true</span>:NoSchedule</code></pre></figure>\n<p>(What a taint is, and how a toleration lets a pod past it: <a href=\"/blog/concepts#taints-and-tolerations\">Concepts: what each piece is</a>.)</p>\n<p><strong>4.3 Node pools: labels and taints.</strong> k3d has no node pools. The Kubernetes equivalent is a label that pods\nselect, and optionally a taint that keeps other pods away.</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20label%20node%20k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-0%20pool%3Dapp%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl label node k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-0 pool=app</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20label%20node%20k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1%20pool%3Ddata%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl label node k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1 pool=data</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20taint%20node%20k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1%20dedicated%3Ddata%3ANoSchedule%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl taint node k3d-local-cluster-1-agent-1 dedicated=data:NoSchedule</code></pre></figure>\n<p>A pod then needs both the selector and the matching toleration to land on the <code>data</code> pool:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"yaml\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">yaml</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"hljs-attr\">spec:</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-attr\">nodeSelector:</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-attr\">pool:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">data</span>\n  <span class=\"hljs-attr\">tolerations:</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-bullet\">-</span> <span class=\"hljs-attr\">key:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">dedicated</span>\n      <span class=\"hljs-attr\">operator:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">Equal</span>\n      <span class=\"hljs-attr\">value:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">data</span>\n      <span class=\"hljs-attr\">effect:</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">NoSchedule</span></code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>4.4 Add and remove nodes live.</strong> This is the part kind cannot do.</p>\n<p>Add a worker:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20node%20create%20extra%20--cluster%20local-cluster-1%20--role%20agent%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d node create extra --cluster local-cluster-1 --role agent</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20nodes%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get nodes</code></pre></figure>\n<p>A new node appears (named <code>k3d-extra-0</code>; <code>k3d node list</code> shows the exact name).</p>\n<p>Remove it. Drain first so its pods move to other nodes:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20drain%20k3d-extra-0%20--ignore-daemonsets%20--delete-emptydir-data%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl drain k3d-extra-0 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20delete%20node%20k3d-extra-0%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl delete node k3d-extra-0</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20node%20delete%20k3d-extra-0%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d node delete k3d-extra-0</code></pre></figure>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-5--namespaces\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-5--namespaces\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 5 — Namespaces</h2>\n<p>Identical to kind:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20create%20namespace%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl create namespace web</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20create%20namespace%20cache%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl create namespace cache</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20create%20namespace%20db%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl create namespace db</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20namespaces%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get namespaces</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>web</code>, <code>cache</code> and <code>db</code> are there, next to the built-in <code>default</code>, <code>kube-system</code>, <code>kube-public</code> and\n<code>kube-node-lease</code>.</p>\n<p>To deploy apps into them (the same commands on k3d), see <a href=\"/blog/deploy-apps\">Deploy apps into your namespaces, one at a time</a>. Use the pool\nlabels from 4.3 instead of kind&#39;s <code>role=data</code> in the <code>nodeSelector</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-6--what-k3d-gives-you-that-kind-does-not\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-6--what-k3d-gives-you-that-kind-does-not\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 6 — What k3d gives you that kind does not</h2>\n<p>k3s bundles most of what a managed cluster provides, so there is little to install:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Table (scrolls sideways)\"><table><thead><tr><th>GKE feature</th><th>Here</th><th>Install needed?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nodes you can add and remove live</td><td><code>k3d node create</code> / <code>k3d node delete</code></td><td>no</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>type: LoadBalancer</code> gets an address</td><td>k3s&#39;s built-in service load balancer, reached through k3d&#39;s load balancer container</td><td>no</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Ingress</td><td>Traefik, bundled with k3s</td><td>no</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Metrics, <code>kubectl top</code>, pod autoscaling</td><td>metrics-server, bundled with k3s</td><td>no</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Persistent volumes</td><td><code>local-path</code> storage class, bundled with k3s</td><td>no</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Container registry (Artifact Registry)</td><td>a registry container k3d creates and wires into the nodes</td><td>one flag</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Node pools</td><td>node labels and taints</td><td>two commands</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Console UI</td><td>Headlamp</td><td>one install</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Node autoscaling, Autopilot, IAM</td><td>not available locally</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"61-reach-an-app-with-ingress-or-a-loadbalancer\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#61-reach-an-app-with-ingress-or-a-loadbalancer\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>6.1 Reach an app with Ingress or a LoadBalancer</h3>\n<p>Deploy something first:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20create%20deployment%20web%20--image%3Dnginx%3A1.27%20--replicas%3D2%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=2 -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20expose%20deployment%20web%20--port%3D80%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl expose deployment web --port=80 -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>Ingress</strong> (Traefik picks it up):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20apply%20-f%20-%20%3C%3C'EOF'%22%2C%22apiVersion%3A%20networking.k8s.io%2Fv1%22%2C%22kind%3A%20Ingress%22%2C%22metadata%3A%22%2C%22%20%20name%3A%20web%22%2C%22%20%20namespace%3A%20web%22%2C%22spec%3A%22%2C%22%20%20rules%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20-%20http%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20paths%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20-%20path%3A%20%2F%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20pathType%3A%20Prefix%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20backend%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20service%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20name%3A%20web%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20port%3A%22%2C%22%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20number%3A%2080%22%2C%22EOF%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;EOF&#x27;</span>\napiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: web\n  namespace: web\nspec:\n  rules:\n    - http:\n        paths:\n          - path: /\n            pathType: Prefix\n            backend:\n              service:\n                name: web\n                port:\n                  number: 80\nEOF</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22curl%20-s%20http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A8080%20%7C%20head%20-5%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>curl -s http://localhost:8080 | <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">head</span> -5</code></pre></figure>\n<p>The nginx page: local port 8080 → load balancer → Traefik → Service → pod.</p>\n<p><strong>LoadBalancer Service</strong> (the GKE-style external address):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20expose%20deployment%20web%20--name%3Dweb-lb%20--type%3DLoadBalancer%20--port%3D80%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl expose deployment web --name=web-lb --<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">type</span>=LoadBalancer --port=80 -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20service%20web-lb%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get service web-lb -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>EXTERNAL-IP</code> fills in with a node address. Port 80 through <code>localhost:8080</code> is already taken by Traefik, so\nfor a second LoadBalancer Service use another port (<code>--port=8081</code>) and add a matching <code>--port</code> mapping when\ncreating the cluster, or just use <code>kubectl port-forward</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"62-metrics-and-pod-autoscaling\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#62-metrics-and-pod-autoscaling\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>6.2 Metrics and pod autoscaling</h3>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20top%20nodes%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl top nodes</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Works after about a minute (metrics-server is bundled). Then autoscale the pods. The autoscaler needs the pods\nto declare a CPU request:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20set%20resources%20deployment%20web%20--requests%3Dcpu%3D50m%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span> resources deployment web --requests=cpu=50m -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20autoscale%20deployment%20web%20--cpu%3D50%25%20--min%3D2%20--max%3D6%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl autoscale deployment web --cpu=50% --min=2 --max=6 -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20get%20hpa%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl get hpa -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Shows current vs target CPU. It adds pods under load, up to 6, and removes them again. That is <strong>pod</strong>\nautoscaling, which works as it does on GKE. Node autoscaling does not exist here.</p>\n<h3 id=\"63-your-own-images\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#63-your-own-images\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>6.3 Your own images</h3>\n<p>Two ways, as in <a href=\"/blog/run-your-image\">Run your own image in the cluster</a>, and both are simpler on k3d.</p>\n<p><strong>Copy the image into the nodes</strong> (the equivalent of <code>kind load</code>):</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20image%20import%20my-app%3Av1%20-c%20local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d image import my-app:v1 -c local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>Or use the registry</strong> created with the cluster. Push from your terminal:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20build%20-t%20localhost%3A5001%2Fmy-app%3Av1%20.%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker build -t localhost:5001/my-app:v1 .</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20push%20localhost%3A5001%2Fmy-app%3Av1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker push localhost:5001/my-app:v1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Inside the cluster the same registry has another name (a node&#39;s <code>localhost</code> is the node itself), and k3d has\nalready set up the mirror on every node. That replaces the manual registry steps in Part 1.2 of\n<a href=\"/blog/run-your-image\">Run your own image in the cluster</a>:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22kubectl%20create%20deployment%20my-app%20--image%3Dk3d-local-registry%3A5000%2Fmy-app%3Av1%20-n%20web%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>kubectl create deployment my-app --image=k3d-local-registry:5000/my-app:v1 -n web</code></pre></figure>\n<h3 id=\"64-dashboard\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#64-dashboard\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>6.4 Dashboard</h3>\n<p>Open Headlamp from Applications. It lists your kubeconfig&#39;s contexts; pick <code>k3d-local-cluster-1</code>. It shows\nnodes, namespaces, pods, logs and events: the nearest thing to the Cloud Console here.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"part-7--stop-start-delete\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#part-7--stop-start-delete\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a>Part 7 — Stop, start, delete</h2>\n<p>Pause the cluster to free memory, and bring it back:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20stop%20local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster stop local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20start%20local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster start local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>Remove the cluster. This also removes its kubectl context:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20delete%20local-cluster-1%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster delete local-cluster-1</code></pre></figure>\n<p>The registry container created with <code>--registry-create</code> may be left behind. Remove it too:</p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20rm%20-f%20k3d-local-registry%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">rm</span> -f k3d-local-registry</code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>Check:</strong></p>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22k3d%20cluster%20list%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>k3d cluster list</code></pre></figure>\n<figure class=\"code\" data-lang=\"bash\"><figcaption><span class=\"lang\">bash</span><a class=\"code-try\" href=\"/app?run=%5B%22docker%20ps%20-a%20--format%20'table%20%7B%7B.Names%7D%7D%5C%5Ct%7B%7B.Status%7D%7D'%22%5D&amp;notour=1\">Try in playground</a><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></figcaption><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code>docker ps -a --format <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;table {{.Names}}\\t{{.Status}}&#x27;</span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>No <code>k3d-…</code> containers should remain. If a stale context is left in your kubeconfig, remove it as in\n<a href=\"/blog/clean-up\">Stop, shut down and clean up</a>, using the name <code>k3d-local-cluster-1</code>.</p>\n"}